{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430543-questions-questions","id":430543,"title":"Questions, questions...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-06T13:39:57-08:00","id":430543,"title":"Questions, questions...","content":"Got a few concerning 1st Ed WtF(edited in some new questions):<br /> <br /> 1. Does gaining a new dot in Renown automatically grant you a gift of the same dot, like rituals do?<b>(Answered)</b><br /> <br /> 2. If you take an AK-47 with you in the Spirit World, do you still have it and does it still work?<b>(Answered)</b><br /> <br /> 3 Can anyone give me examples of a Tur (meeting places for packs) and activities that go on there? Is there any book treating this?<b>(Answered)</b><br /> <br /> 4. How do phases of the moon work(a lunar cycle has about 30 days, does each auspice get 5 days, or is it three days for each auspice with some leftover days)?<br /> <br /> 5. Can you get a two dot gift if you haven't bought the one-dot gift preceding it?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://multiversalmoments.weebly.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://multiversalmoments.weebly.com/</a>","edited":{"userid":2603,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2603-iamthenight","user":"iamthenight","date":".  New questions 03-09-2015, 08:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2603-iamthenight","name":"iamthenight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T14:36:11-08:00","id":430623,"title":"","content":"1. Yes<br /> <br /> 2. You'd need to use the Rite of Dedication on it first.<br /> <br /> 3. No idea, lets let someone else answer that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T14:47:04-08:00","id":430629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>iamthenight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430543-questions-questions#post430543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3 Can anyone give me examples of a Tur (meeting places for packs) and activities that go on there? Is there any book treating this?</div> </div> </div> </div>I just remember one, it's been a while. It was at an open area in a national park for a night or two, lots of werewolves from around the state and other areas went there. Some were looking for new packs to join up with. Others were discussing the Pure threat, which most deemed nonexistent. Some were there to settle old feuds. There was a sort of wrestling tournament that got out of control. In the 'random encounter' department there was also a couple, twins, one of whom ended up giving birth to a <i>unihar</i>. It sort of spoiled the mood, especially as so many werewolves tried to jump on it to little avail.<br /> <br /> It's in a different gameline, but <i>Invite Only</i> is Vampire the Requiem's guide for creating an Elysium, a sort of organized vampire gathering. I'm unaware if there is a Werewolf equivalent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T16:05:18-08:00","id":430747,"title":"","content":"Something to consider regarding the AK-47 and the Shadow - Depending on your ST, you may have to dedicate the rifle and the clip inside as one 'dedicated' item and any more ammunition separately. Technically though you could put the gun, magazines &amp; anything else you fancy into a bag and dedicate the bag and its contents as one item, but that's open to interpretation I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4910-warrior-angel","name":"warrior angel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4910_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T05:38:37-07:00","id":433811,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the bump...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://multiversalmoments.weebly.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://multiversalmoments.weebly.com/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2603-iamthenight","name":"iamthenight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T05:50:08-07:00","id":433817,"title":"","content":"You could have just slapped those extra questions in the new post, you know. <br /> <br /> Anyway, to answer:<br /> <br /> &quot;Full moon&quot; is the actual night of full moon and the two days either side. LIkewise &quot;New Moon&quot; is the new moon and the two days either side of that. For the other auspices it's each gibbous, half or crescent and <i>one</i> day either side. So full and new get five days of auspice moon in a row once a month, while the other three get three days in a row twice a month. <br /> <br /> You can buy gifts out of order but it costs an extra thee experience points for each one you skipped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T08:25:16-07:00","id":434080,"title":"","content":"You can get a gift without the one(s) preceding it in two ways. One, if you get a dot of renown, the free gift that accompanies it can be from a list in which you have no previous gifts. (ex. getting dot 3 in Honor, you could choose the 3 dot gift Echo Dream to accompany it even if you don't have any of the earlier gifts in the Insight gift tree).<br /> <br /> And two, you can just purchase the gift straight out, paying an extra 3 experience for every gift you skipped to get it. (So assuming it was an affinity gift for you, the three dot gift Echo Dream would normally cost 15 experience if you already had both the earlier gift in the tree, but if you didn't, it'd cost 3+3+15)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}